쓰레기로 만든 바이올린 (80s Cel Anime version) — credits and licences

Film: made entirely in code with the Lemo-Opuscar library (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT), 80s Cel Anime style.
  cel.js, head80.js, post.js and fx.js are adapted from the style's demo engine (MIT).
Music: original composition (this project). No third-party melody.
  Samples (CC0 1.0): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios); Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios).
Sound effects and ambience: synthesised procedurally (this project), no recordings.
Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, via Google Fonts, subset to the characters used): Gothic A1 (HanYang I&C), Black Han Sans (Zess Type).

Story: based on the true story of the Recycled Orchestra of Cateura (Orquesta de Instrumentos Reciclados de Cateura), Paraguay.
  Facts were checked against public reporting and the 2013 "Landfill Harmonic" trailer; no footage, images, compositions,
  interview audio or dialogue from any source are used. The girl and the children are composite characters, not real people.
  The subtitle "쓰레기도, 사람도. 함부로 버려져선 안 된다." paraphrases in Korean a remark by conductor Favio Chávez in that trailer.
Suggested description line: 파라과이 카테우라 재활용 오케스트라의 실화를 바탕으로 재구성한 애니메이션입니다. 영상 속 아이들은 단원들을 대표하는 가상 인물입니다.
